# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# This tree is assembled on Windows and runs on Linux. Without this, a commit made on a
# Windows checkout can store CRLF in a file that CI executes as a shell script, and the
# failure is confusing out of proportion to its cause: `\r` becomes part of the last
# argument on every line.
#
# `* text=auto` tells git to normalise on commit; the explicit entries below leave no doubt
# for the files where a stray CR actually breaks something.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh      text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.toml    text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*    text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf

# Binary: never normalise, never diff as text.
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.gif     binary
*.ico     binary
*.pdf     binary
*.gguf    binary
*.safetensors binary
*.onnx    binary
